    {
      "id": "l2bil9n",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Definition of Narration"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Direct speech quotes the exact words spoken, while indirect speech conveys the substance of the speech without exact words.",
        "Converting direct to indirect speech involves systematic updates to tenses, pronouns, and words indicating time and place.",
        "Interrogative sentences require changing reporting verbs to 'asked' or 'enquired' and using appropriate conjunctions like 'if' or 'whether'.",
        "Imperative sentences convert main verbs into infinitives paired with verbs like 'ordered', 'requested', or 'advised'."
      ],
      "id": "snj4adx"
    },
